open_obligations.partial_result:
The unchanged-class bracket already established in \(\texttt{thm:test-optimization-not-sharp}\) remains
\[
 c n^{-2\gamma/(4\gamma+d)}\leq\rho_n^*\leq Cb_n,
 \;
 b_n=\begin{cases}
 n^{-2t/(4t+d)},&d\leq4t,\\
 n^{-4t/(4t+3d)},&d>4t,
 \end{cases}
 \; t=\min\{\gamma,\alpha+\beta\},
 \tag{34}
\]
for all sufficiently large \(n\).  If \(\alpha+\beta\geq\gamma\) and \(d\leq4\gamma\), then \(\rho_n^*\asymp\rho_{n,e}^*\asymp n^{-2\gamma/(4\gamma+d)}\), with no logarithm at \(d=4\gamma\).

For the mandated four-atom nested prior at \(d=\gamma=1\), \(\alpha=\beta=1/10\), \(h\asymp\delta^5\), \(H\asymp\delta\), and \(\delta=\epsilon n^{-3/10}\), the exact \(2+1\) canonical contribution is \(\Theta(\epsilon^{10})=O(\epsilon^4)\), so it is not the obstruction at this revised scale.  The exact \(2+3\) fifth canonical projection is \(\delta^4\mathcal L_{12}\kappa_3\kappa_4\kappa_5\), and its squared likelihood contribution is at least \(c_b(n)_5hH^3\delta^8\asymp c_b\epsilon^{16}n^{1/5}\).  Therefore the proposed support-controlled \(L^2\) connected-cluster remainder does not close for this four-atom prior.  A different bounded constant-null-supported prior, an additional cancellation, or a direct Hellinger comparison that avoids the divergent second likelihood moment is required.  Independently, the canonical \(2+1\) collision statistic still needs a deterministic alternative dichotomy, signal-dependent projection bounds, uniform finite-sample calibration, and all-regime optimization before it yields a repaired upper map.  The frozen \(r_{\mathrm{mix}}\) and \(r_{\mathrm{test}}\) remain diagnostics, and no common sharp-rate symbol is defined.
